  "summary": "I wrote the breakout game in src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it in a browser here, so the gameplay, rendering and `vite build` are untested.\n\n- **Play field:** the 3D scene has walls, a ceiling, a paddle and a ball. There are 8×5 bricks, one colour per row, worth 50, 40, 30, 20 and 10 points from the top row down.\n- **Controls:** Left/Right arrows or A/D move the paddle, Space serves and R restarts at any time.\n- **Ball:** it bounces off the walls, ceiling, paddle and bricks. The paddle sets the ball's horizontal direction by where it is hit, up to 60° from vertical.\n- **Lives and status:** there are 3 lives. A missed ball re-serves from the paddle on Space, and 0 lives gives `lost`. Clearing every brick gives `won`.\n- **HUD:** a DOM bar under the canvas shows score, lives and status. A full-canvas overlay with an \"R to restart\" hint appears on win or loss.\n- **Exposed state:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a getter returning `{ status, score, lives, bricksLeft }`.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__TASK_READY__` is set to `true` on the second rendered frame.\n\nI added a small help line under the HUD that lists the controls.\n\n",
